{
  "suite": "oidc-delivery",
  "title": "A push authenticated by an OIDC bearer token (Google Cloud Pub/Sub)",
  "contract": {
    "summary": "`verifyOidcDelivery` (TS) / `OidcDelivery::verify` (PHP): refuse when the host configured no keys, audience or principal; read `Bearer <token>` from the scheme's header (header name and auth scheme case-insensitive); verify the JWT with `verifyJwt` / `Jwt::verify` (RS256, kid, exp, nbf, the scheme's issuers, the configured audience, 60 s leeway); then require the scheme's principalClaim to EQUAL the configured principal and its verifiedClaim to be the literal true. Reasons are fixed strings; a JWT refusal passes through unchanged.",
    "reference": "authored",
    "referenceNote": "Claims follow Google's documented example (aud, azp, email, email_verified, exp, iat, iss, sub; tokens up to an hour old). Google publishes no verifiable token, so rows are signed by a throwaway 2048-bit key generated when this table was written; only its PUBLIC JWK is stored. 0012 is signed by a second throwaway key."
  },
